# Test-first (TDD)

When the work is (or should be) covered by automated tests:

1. Write / update the failing test first
2. Run it and confirm it fails for the right reason
3. Implement the minimal change to make it pass
4. Re-run the test(s)

## Applies when

- Changing behavior of code that already has tests
- Adding behavior that the project normally covers with unit/integration tests (UI primitives, utils, hooks, etc.)

## Does not apply when

- Pure docs, tokens/CSS-only visual tweaks without behavioral contract
- Exploratory spikes where the user explicitly asked to skip tests
- Changes outside the project's usual test surface
